  "id": "COMPOUND:3938 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Methylmalonic Acid may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Methylmalonic Acid to EDD domain proteins in the DegV family, which are targets of Itaconic Anhydride. The second pathway connects Methylmalonic Acid to Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, which is a target of Acetamide. Both pathways ultimately lead to the activation of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. These findings indicate that Methylmalonic Acid may act as a modulator of the kinase through different molecular intermediates. The evidence is consistent with a regulatory role for Methylmalonic Acid in the activation of this kinase, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
